  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In 5e D&D, most characters will start with a handful of skill proficiencies from Race, Class, and Background and never learn any new skills over the course of their career. Those that do wish to learn something new have two options, multiclassing or feats. This article will be focusing on those feat options for gaining proficiencies as well as touching on other feats that grant skill related bonuses."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "There are three feats that grant skill proficiencies, Skilled, Skill Expert, and Prodigy, as well as a handful of feats that grant non-proficiency bonuses to skills. We’ll discuss in depth the pros and cons of the first three, and then briefly compare the benefits of the other feats to simply gaining Expertise from Skill Expert."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For further reading and inspiration on ways to apply skills and tools in your games, we recommend reading the other articles in this series, "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "The Practical Guide to Tools",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/tools/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", and "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "The Practical Guide to Impractical Skill Checks",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/impractical-skill-checks/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
